enue per employee of $615K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers, improving at 27%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $155K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Lexicon Pharmaceuticals, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $792M market cap on $50M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +28% over the past three years and -9% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -139% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $68M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at +9.5% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -5.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 25% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-9.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 99% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented indus